        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "A timestamp is (l, c): max wall time seen, plus a logical counter.",
      "narration": "An HLC timestamp is a pair. L tracks the largest physical time seen. C is a counter that breaks ties when L does not advance.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Timestamp = (l, c)",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "l: highest wall time seen so far",
            "c: counter when l did not advance",
            "Compare l first, then c"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "s",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "Timestamp {\n  WallTime int64\n  Logical  int32 }",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 54,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 3500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "src",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "CockroachDB: pkg/util/hlc",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 76,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 5500,
          "enter": "fade",
          "color": "purple"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 12000,
      "caption": "On a local event or send, take max(l, pt); bump c only on a tie.",
      "narration": "On a local event or send, set L to the max of its old value and the physical clock. If L did not move, increment C. Otherwise reset C to zero.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Local event / send",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "l_old = l\nl = max(l_old, pt)\nif l == l_old: c++\nelse:          c = 0",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Time never goes backwards, even if pt does.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 52,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 4000,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 6000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "caption": "On receive, also fold in the message timestamp, so causality holds.",
      "narration": "On receive, L becomes the max of local, message, and physical time. The counter then continues from whichever side shares that L.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Receive message",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "text": "l = max(l_old, m.l, pt)\nif l==l_old==m.l:\n  c = max(c, m.c) + 1\nelif l==l_old: c++\nelif l==m.l: c = m.c + 1\nelse: c = 0",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "n",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The result is always greater than both inputs.",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 56,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 5000,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "c",
          "at": 7000,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "caption": "l stays within the clock-skew bound of real time, and c stays small.",
      "narration": "Because L follows physical time, it stays within the skew bound of a real clock, while still ordering causally related events.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "h",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "What you get",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 6,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 0,
          "enter": "fade"
        },
        {
          "id": "l",
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "e causes f implies hlc(e) < hlc(f)",
            "l stays close to real time",
            "Fixed-size, so cheap to store"
          ],
          "x": 8,
          "y": 22,
          "w": 84,
          "at": 500,
          "enter": "slide-up"
        },
        {
          "id": "f",
          "type": "highlight",
          "target": "l",
          "at": 4500,
          "enter": "fade"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "takeaway": "An HLC is (max wall time seen, counter): causal like Lamport, yet always close to real time and constant-size.",
